Requirements
Install the required libraries:
pip install pybullet
Python version:
•	Python 3.7 or higher
________________________________________
Step 1: URDF Robot Model
The robot is fully described using URDF, including:
•	Visual geometry
•	Collision geometry
•	Inertial properties
•	Joint definitions
The URDF file:
wheeled_robot.urdf
This file defines the kinematic and physical structure of the robot.
________________________________________
Step 2: Launch Robot in PyBullet
Script:
launch_urdf_pybullet.py
Run:
python launch_urdf_pybullet.py
This step:
•	Initializes PyBullet in GUI mode
•	Loads a ground plane
•	Loads the robot model
•	Displays the robot in the simulation window
________________________________________
Step 3: Configure Robot Properties
Script:
configure_robot_properties.py
This step configures:
•	Gravity: −9.81 m/s²
•	Wheel friction: High (for traction)
•	Caster friction: Low (for smooth rolling)
•	Linear and angular damping
•	Base link friction
These parameters ensure:
•	Numerical stability
•	Realistic contact dynamics
•	Smooth motion
________________________________________
